{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "def find_zero(xs: list):\n    # Derivative of polynomial with coefficients xs\n    def poly_derivative(xs, x):\n        return sum([coeff * i * math.pow(x, i - 1) for i, coeff in enumerate(xs) if i > 0])\n    \n    # Newton-Raphson method\n    # Start with an initial guess\n    x = 0.0\n    \n    # Iterate until convergence\n    for _ in range(1000):  # Maximum iterations\n        fx = poly(xs, x)\n        fpx = poly_derivative(xs, x)\n        \n        # Avoid division by zero\n        if abs(fpx) < 1e-10:\n            x += 0.1  # Perturb if derivative is too small\n            continue\n        \n        x_new = x - fx / fpx\n        \n        # Check for convergence\n        if abs(x_new - x) < 1e-10:\n            return x_new\n        \n        x = x_new\n    \n    return x"}
